    "theme": "The qualifying start",
    "narrative": "Baamonde is the 102 km mark, just over the Compostela minimum. New pilgrims arrive here by bus today to start walking tomorrow. The tree-lined square by the Parga river is quiet, the 12th-century Romanesque church (Santiago de Baamonde — a Saint James church welcoming pilgrims walking his way) is worn and loved, and the albergue is full. The atmosphere for long-distance pilgrims is bittersweet — the end is close but so is the crowding. You are a veteran now, whether or not you knew that was coming.",
